# AGENT.md — src/

Application root for the Microservices architecture.

## What lives here

- `main.ts` — starts the gateway{{#if hasOrm}} and initializes the ORM connection{{/if}}.
- `server.ts` — builds the Hapi gateway (initGateway factory), registers plugins
  and initializes all services, then mounts their routes.
- `config/` — environment loading (`env.ts` is the only file that reads `process.env`).
- `plugins/` — Hapi plugin registrations (swagger{{#if useAuth}}, auth{{/if}}).
- `errors/` — AppError base class and subclasses (NotFoundError, ValidationError).
- `shared/` — cross-cutting infrastructure (database, cache{{#if useAuth}}, auth{{/if}}{{#if useHealthCheck}}, health{{/if}}).
- `services/<name>/` — one directory per microservice. Each contains its own
  routes, persistence, entities, and DTOs.

## Service pattern

Each service exports `init<Name>Service() → Promise<{ routes: ServerRoute[] }>`.
The gateway calls this, then mounts `service.routes` via `server.route()`.

Services are isolated — they do not import from each other. Cross-cutting
concerns (auth, db, cache) go through `src/shared/` or `src/plugins/`.

## Rules

- Do not put business logic in `main.ts` or `server.ts`.
- When you add a new service, call its init function and mount its routes
  in `server.ts`.
- Plugins (swagger, auth) are registered in `server.ts` via
  `await server.register([...])`.
- Cross-cutting error formatting uses `server.ext('onPreResponse', ...)`.
{{#if useAuth}}
- Auth is set up as a JWT strategy in `plugins/auth.ts`.
{{/if}}
